// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
// discard.bash's arguments and help (mise run release:discard --help). mise rewraps the help to
// the terminal but keeps its line breaks: a paragraph, or a list's item, is one line.

long_about """
    Delete the images of a release that the Release workflow did not finish. The workflow runs it when a run fails or is cancelled.

    The workflow publishes the images before it tags the release, so that a run that fails leaves no tag. This removes what such a run published: the image tagged with the version, and the image of each architecture.

    It deletes nothing if origin has the release's tag: then the release is made, and the images are its own.

    It is a cleanup only. A run of the same version replaces the images anyway.
    """

after_long_help "GH_TOKEN must be able to delete the package's versions. The workflow's token can, if the repository has the Admin role in the package's settings (Manage Actions access)."

arg "<version>" env="VERSION" help="The release's version: 2026.11.0"
flag "--repo <repo>" env="GH_REPO" required=#true help="The GitHub repository: kludgeworks/eu-legislation-viewer"
flag "--image <image>" env="IMAGE" default="ghcr.io/kludgeworks/eu-legislation-viewer" help="The image's name"

example "mise run release:discard 2026.11.20 --repo kludgeworks/eu-legislation-viewer" header="Delete the images of a release not made" help="As the Release workflow does when a run fails"
